//// actions — the server-action protocol (decision 116 rule 2): the texts a
//// server action writes and a browser reads, and back. One implementation,
//// compiled for erlang and commonJS, so the two sides cannot drift.
////
//// No wire NAME is built in: the hidden form field and the header that name an
//// action are the deployment's values, passed to both sides by whoever wires
//// them. This library holds only the texts whose shape is fixed.

pub mod state;
pub mod envelope;
pub mod rpc;
pub mod refresh;
